  %% 009 ADR-001 as a DECISION MAP: what each decision owns, what it delegates, and
  %% which parts are blocked or not yet independently verified.
  %% Colour = role. Dashed amber = blocked, or not citable as name-adoption gate evidence.
  %% Grounded 2026-08-01 at 81b0a899c9338a63a6abfe08172ee6cb15d313ec, after the fourth
  %% correction pass. Status is Proposed: nothing decided here exists at HEAD.
  %% This is the OVERVIEW for project 009. Three detail views expand it without repeating it:
  %%   dst-model-step-widening   - the one Ports field the whole near-term plan turns on.
  %%   dst-hermeticity-detectors - D4's clock set and D5's three audit obligations.
  %%   dst-trace-and-oracle      - D6-D8 and D11: the returned trace as the oracle.
  %% The system these decisions build is drawn in ../../007_dst_consolidation/mmd/dst-target-system.

  subgraph LINEAGE["lineage — this ADR does not stand alone"]
    direction LR
    dep007["<b>depends on</b> 007 ADR-001 · <i>Accepted 2026-07-26</i><br/>owns the definition, scope, and the naming gate<br/>this ADR owns the mechanism that meets it"]:::note
    am001["<b>amends</b> 001 ADR-001<br/>production-code, explicit-fake, normalized-trace,<br/>stable-scenario, and invariant decisions stay in force ·<br/>scripted results + normalized traces are <i>not</i> a world"]:::note
    am004["<b>amends</b> 004 ADR-001 for the generated axis<br/>pure decide, phase transitions, driver-owned effects,<br/>append-only ledger, extension-resident policy stay in force ·<br/>function-valued ports are no longer the whole state mechanism ·<br/>004's stream-delta ledger-append handle is replaced as<br/><b>unbuildable</b>, its Phase-B byte-parity test relocated"]:::note
  end

  subgraph BLOCK["two acceptance blockers — different in kind"]
    direction LR
    b1["<b>1 · external substrate, not clearable here</b><br/>the upstream recorded-stream API is specified and agreed<br/>but not in a released binary · upstream reproduced the<br/>constraint first-party and recommends adopting this project's<br/>reference implementation with its chunks + outcome shape<br/>the design question is settled; a <b>release event</b> is not<br/><i>a fork prototype does not satisfy D1</i>"]:::blocked
    b2["<b>2 · internal and open</b><br/>the fourth correction pass — the extension-model-path exclusion,<br/>the concrete ProviderState and its module home, the live/Ported<br/>identity contract, the profile-reachable clause for hook-guarded<br/>core paths, and obligation 2's enumerated classifier —<br/>post-dates the two delta reviews and is <b>unverified</b><br/><i>D5's routing audit is not citable until a delta review passes</i>"]:::blocked
  end

  d1["<b>D1 · one driver-owned, state-threaded world protocol</b><br/>handle · world_state + world_request → ordered intermediate emissions ·<br/>response · next_world_state · observations, or a typed HarnessError<br/>seven request kinds · every request returns its successor explicitly, on error too<br/><br/><b>world_state is the only owner of every cursor</b> — not SharedMem, not a global,<br/>not an ambient RNG, not a mutable singleton, and <i>not re-derived from message history</i><br/>interim home: one explicit C2LoopState field, subsumed by world_state and deleted<br/>the world ends at the external result boundary — production still validates,<br/>correlates, converts, and records"]:::seam

  d1blk["<b>streaming parity is the blocked half of D1</b><br/>the spike dispositioned both candidate shapes against pinned v0.26.0:<br/>a modeled provider result has no real API; a scoped SharedMem recorder<br/>is rejected by the callback's closed IO row; a state-returning callback<br/>fails unification against unit · v0.30.0 and v0.31.0 preserve both contracts<br/><i>this blocks parity, not the port widening — see dst-model-step-widening</i>"]:::blocked

  d2["<b>D2 · discovery is seed-driven; replay consumes a resolved program</b><br/>predicting requests would mean duplicating the session logic, so discovery<br/>answers each <i>real</i> request as production makes it, and each choice changes<br/>which request arrives next · replay never calls the generator<br/><br/>DiscoveryConfig → ExecutionProgram · six interaction kinds plus<br/>ExpectExtensionEffect, which closes the class D1/D3/D5 would otherwise<br/>make unreplayable · strict vs regression replay · pure structural validation<br/>every interaction carries a causal identity with a global encounter ordinal<br/>and a bounded request projection"]:::gen

  d3["<b>D3 · logical faults are modeled outcomes, not injected decisions</b><br/>provider · tool · approval · conformant extension effect<br/>the mapping is a <b>versioned machine-readable catalogue the gate reads</b>:<br/>class id · applicability condition · delivered constructor ·<br/><b>named recovery-branch id</b> · logical state transition<br/>every outcome defines its logical world transition — timeout may not<br/>leave logical state ambiguous<br/>two classes are conditional; a profile that skips them must <b>name the waiver</b><br/><i>forcing StepDecision, editing ledger state, or bypassing validation is rejected</i>"]:::fault

  d4["<b>D4 · one monotonic virtual clock, and it is the only clock</b><br/>the explicit value in world_state is authoritative — no runtime epoch,<br/>no mirrored advance, no conformance assertion against a runtime value<br/><b>this is a correction:</b> pinned --virtual-time prints a banner and changes<br/>nothing — now() returns real epoch and sleep blocks for real time<br/>timeout is derived from generated completion time against a production<br/>deadline, never a freely chosen error label<br/>modeled time is free, so determinism no longer trades against gate runtime<br/><i>routing is all-or-nothing within a profile — see dst-hermeticity-detectors</i>"]:::clock

  d5["<b>D5 · the real traced driver, under a named conformant profile</b><br/>run_v2_session_traced or a successor · the message-only entry point is not the oracle<br/><b>profile</b> (semantic, versioned) + <b>manifest</b> (per run: revision, toolchain, packages, ABI)<br/>a hook is covered only if effect-free, or effectful only through world-mediated<br/>ports with explicit state returned · an excluded hook that is <i>reached</i> fails closed,<br/>so a seed cannot buy coverage by missing it<br/>test-only code may generate, decode, simulate, and assert — it may not reimplement<br/>transitions, recovery policy, tool history, compaction, or finalization"]:::driver

  d5open["<b>obligation 2 is a repair the authoring side wrote</b><br/>converged on by both delta reviews, verified by neither"]:::blocked

  d6["<b>D6 · every run returns one complete terminal trace</b><br/>two disjoint classes: SystemRun and HarnessFailure<br/>exactly one canonical RunSummary as the final record — <b>zero at HEAD on every path</b><br/>parity, not a shared transition: stream emissions are the named exception<br/><b>the event vocabulary is the fifth versioned axis</b> — variant, wire name,<br/>payload schema, and logical vs display-only classification, which exists nowhere today"]:::out

  d7["<b>D7 · invariants are evaluated over the whole execution</b><br/>one final RunSummary · logical-emission parity · legal transitions · tool-call pairing ·<br/>budget monotonicity · bounded retry · outcome/summary agreement · strict-replay equality ·<br/>valid logical-world transitions · monotonic virtual time · zero forbidden effects<br/><b>the discovery contract is itself an invariant</b>: the same manifest, profile, and seed<br/>run twice must yield the same program, log, outcome, and normalized trace<br/><i>a generated run that checks only final prose or a golden snapshot is not this axis</i>"]:::oracle

  d8["<b>D8 · replay records the program, not just the seed</b><br/>a seed identifies code, not a failure — the exact serialized program is the durable unit<br/>every failure preserves schema, generator id/version, seed, program, revision, toolchain,<br/>profile + manifest, <b>event-vocabulary version</b>, first failed invariant, outcome, trace<br/>the reproducibility promise is conditioned on the recorded manifest and profile<br/>a PRNG, draw-order, range, or default-world change that can remap a seed<br/>requires a generator-version bump, enforced by a pinned canary<br/>shrinking operates on programs, preserving causality and revalidating each reduction"]:::artifact

  d11["<b>D11 · search is a first-class gate</b><br/>a blocking PR corpus of fixed seeds and promoted regressions, plus a<br/>rotating scheduled corpus with a deterministic seed window<br/>each declares an operator-accepted minimum the gate asserts exactly —<br/>zero, truncated, or below-minimum fails<br/><b>class-reached and branch-reached are separate counters</b> read from D3's<br/>catalogue: reaching a fault class is not evidence its production branch ran<br/>a promoted failure travels <b>with its manifest</b>, or it is a program nobody<br/>can state the meaning of"]:::artifact

  d9["<b>D9 · sequential until the production contract changes</b><br/>one interaction at a time, one explicit world state, no scheduler<br/>revisit before parallel ledger-affecting tools, ledger-sharing<br/>subagents, state-mutating background callbacks, or independently<br/>state-advancing stream handlers — adding concurrency without<br/>revisiting invalidates the model"]:::rule

  d10["<b>D10 · naming changes only at the conformance gate</b><br/>fixed scenarios, seeded scalar PBT, conformance tests, and live<br/>smokes remain and test different things<br/>new targets use a non-simulation working name until the<br/>acceptance test passes for a documented baseline profile"]:::rule

  gate{"<b>the acceptance test for the name</b><br/>eleven questions, each answered by an <i>automated</i> gate:<br/>one seed generates an execution, not values · the environment is modeled ·<br/>the boundary is honest · faults reach mapped recovery branches · virtual time matters ·<br/>production logic is under test · the oracle is complete · harness failures are separate ·<br/>discovery and replay are stable · hermeticity is enforced · search actually happens"}:::decision

  earned["<b>Motoko single-actor, logical-fault DST</b><br/>under the named profile and recorded manifest — never a claim<br/>that every installable extension is hermetic<br/><i>no target adopts the name merely because this ADR exists</i>"]:::mode

